Subject: Cantor Phase3 Topology Machine Forms Exploded Specification

@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Machine_Forms.sop

& [BoundaryAxis] separates syntax from truth
  + [valid_form] is structurally coherent caller evidence
  + [admitted_topology] requires the absent M2C scanner and policy
  + [consumed_once] requires the absent supervisor ledger

& [IdentityAxis] is fixed-width and scan-local
  + [volume] is u64
  + [file] is 16 bytes represented by 32 lowercase hex characters

& [EntryAxis] is a three-row coherence table
  + [root] has no relative path, directory mode, and no content fields
  + [directory] has a relative path, directory mode, and no content fields
  + [regular] has a relative path, regular mode, length, and digest

& [StreamAxis] is ordered and unambiguous
  + [default] is exactly ::$DATA
  + [named] is every other admitted bounded name
  + [collection] is sorted, unique, bounded, and has at most one default

& [FreshnessAxis] is half-open
  + [receipt] requires issued_tick less than expires_tick
  + [consumption] requires issued_tick less than or equal to consumed_tick less than expires_tick

& [FaultAxis] couples uncertainty to disposition
  + [pre_change] may deny launch
  + [possible_change] quarantines
  + [observed_change] explicitly quarantines

& [PurityAxis] is inspectable
  + [imports] are fmt and serde only
  + [inputs] are caller-owned values and JSON bytes
  + [effects] are absent
